# `comms::CarrierResult`

The result of carrier recovery.

## Signature

```cpp
comms::CarrierResult
```

## What It Does

Holds the corrected symbols and the phase the loop tracked for each.

## Fields

| Field | Meaning | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `symbols` | The symbols after the tracked phase is removed, `[..., N]`. |  |
| `phase` | The phase estimate used for every symbol, in radians, `[..., N]`. |  |

## Returns

Returned by `pll`.

## Errors

Reading a field does not run the loop again.

## Interpretation and Use

The phase starts at zero and converges; the first symbols of a block are not yet corrected. The phase is only known modulo `2 pi / order`.

